From: dotlouis <1891109+dotlouis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:15:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/41] MTROPOLIS: Fix the loop and visible attribute IDs of
 Set Attribute messages

The attribute name table mapped the "visible" attribute ID to "loop",
overwriting its own "visible" entry, and the "loop" ID wasn't mapped at
all. Messengers setting "loop" failed, which left the failing task on
the VThread and stopped the runtime for good, and messengers setting
"visible" changed "loop" instead.

Uncle Albert's Fabulous Voyage sets "loop" this way when entering a
notebook page, which froze the game in the middle of the page turn.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp b/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp
index 02a1a22da39..5e28846cf3a 100644
--- a/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp
+++ b/engines/mtropolis/runtime.cpp
@@ -4589,7 +4589,7 @@ Runtime::Runtime(OSystem *system, Audio::Mixer *mixer, ISaveUIProvider *saveProv
 	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribVisible] = "visible";
 	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribLayer] = "layer";
 	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribPaused] = "paused";
-	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribVisible] = "loop";
+	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribLoop] = "loop";
 	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribPosition] = "position";
 	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribWidth] = "width";
 	_getSetAttribIDsToAttribName[AttributeIDs::kAttribHeight] = "height";
